{%- comment -%}
  The Chum who is always there.

  A small Chum strolls along the bottom of the viewport on every page, turns
  around at each end, and bobs as she goes.

  Built to cost nothing, because it is on screen permanently and the scroll was
  only just made smooth:
    - CSS animation only. No rAF loop, no scroll listener, no JS at all.
    - transform only — translateX for the walk, translateY/rotate for the bob.
      Both are compositor properties, so this never triggers layout or paint.
    - No filter, no blend mode. Those are the two things that forced per-frame
      re-rasterising elsewhere in this theme.
    - Two nested elements so the walk and the bob own separate transforms
      instead of fighting over one.
    - pointer-events:none, so it can never swallow a tap meant for the page.

  It walks the LEFT side only: the WhatsApp button lives bottom-right and the
  two must not meet.

  Params:
    chum  asset filename. Default gc3-nain-back.webp.

  Why the BACK view: the hero already stands dhi-peace, tara-stand and
  nain-stand across the bottom of the homepage, all facing front. A fourth
  front-facing Chum walking past them read as the same character duplicated.
  Seen from behind he is plainly a different element — someone strolling
  through — and the pose is the only one of the eight that suits walking.
{%- endcomment -%}
{%- assign chum = chum | default: 'gc3-nain-back.webp' -%}
{%- comment -%} must match the file: gc3-nain-back.webp is 330x760, not the 554 Tara is {%- endcomment -%}
{%- assign chum_w = chum_w | default: 330 -%}
<style>
  /* Hidden and PAUSED until he is let in. The homepage hero already stands
     three Chums across the bottom of the viewport, and a fourth walking
     through them read as a collision rather than as company. Paused, not just
     transparent, so an off-screen animation is not being ticked for nothing. */
  .gc-buddy{position:fixed;left:0;bottom:calc(var(--buddy-w) * -0.10);z-index:40;pointer-events:none;
    width:var(--buddy-w);height:auto;line-height:0;
    will-change:transform;opacity:0;transition:opacity .45s ease;
    animation:gcBuddyWalk 34s linear infinite;animation-play-state:paused}
  .gc-buddy.is-on{opacity:1;animation-play-state:running}
  .gc-buddy__in{display:block;line-height:0;
    animation:gcBuddyBob 1.7s ease-in-out infinite alternate}
  .gc-buddy img{display:block;width:100%;height:auto;
    -webkit-user-drag:none;user-select:none;-webkit-touch-callout:none}

  /* Smaller on a phone, where the bottom-left corner is where prices and
     meta lines sit. He also sinks slightly past the edge so he reads as
     walking ALONG the bottom rather than standing on top of the content. */
  :root{--buddy-w:clamp(56px,7vw,104px)}

  /* The walk: out to the far end, turn, back, turn. scaleX flips her at the
     exact frame she stops, so she always faces the way she is going. The
     distance is the viewport minus her own width and the gutter, so she never
     clips off the edge and never reaches the WhatsApp button. */
  @keyframes gcBuddyWalk{
    0%   {transform:translateX(var(--gutter)) scaleX(1)}
    46%  {transform:translateX(calc(52vw - var(--buddy-w))) scaleX(1)}
    50%  {transform:translateX(calc(52vw - var(--buddy-w))) scaleX(-1)}
    96%  {transform:translateX(var(--gutter)) scaleX(-1)}
    100% {transform:translateX(var(--gutter)) scaleX(1)}
  }
  @keyframes gcBuddyBob{
    from{transform:translateY(0) rotate(-2.2deg)}
    to  {transform:translateY(-7px) rotate(2.2deg)}
  }

  /* Short screens have no room for a walking figure over the content. */
  @media (max-height:560px){.gc-buddy{display:none}}
  @media (prefers-reduced-motion:reduce){
    .gc-buddy{animation:none;transform:translateX(var(--gutter))}
    .gc-buddy__in{animation:none}
  }
</style>

<div class="gc-buddy" aria-hidden="true">
  <span class="gc-buddy__in">
    <img src="{{ chum | asset_url }}" alt="" width="{{ chum_w }}" height="760" loading="lazy" decoding="async" draggable="false">
  </span>
</div>

<script>
(function(){
  var b = document.querySelector('.gc-buddy');
  if (!b) return;
  /* Only the homepage has the standing Chums. Everywhere else he walks on
     straight away. */
  var hero = document.querySelector('.gh-stage') || document.querySelector('.gh-pin');
  if (!hero || !('IntersectionObserver' in window)) { b.classList.add('is-on'); return; }
  /* One observer, no scroll listener: this fires twice on the whole page —
     once when the hero leaves, once if it comes back — and costs nothing in
     between. */
  new IntersectionObserver(function (entries) {
    b.classList.toggle('is-on', !entries[0].isIntersecting);
  }, { threshold: 0 }).observe(hero);
})();
</script>
